{
  "_comment": "Hand-authored fixture for tuple returns. Mirrors the layout juliac emits for `JLWResult{CNTuple{2,T}}`, with two @ccallable functions returning one, plus the macro-emitted jlw_free/jlw_free_strings release entrypoints so the owning elements are `:auto` (copy, then free in a `finally`), not `:mechanical`. `stats` returns a tuple of two different types, which juliac emits as a struct whose fields are the positions `1` and `2`, and whose first element owns its storage and second does not, so the emitter has to convert the two by different kinds and release only the first. `pair` returns a tuple of two of one type, which juliac emits as an inline array reached by position instead. Offsets probed from the real JLWInterop layout: sizeof(CNTuple{2, Tuple{CVector{:owned,Float64},Int64}})=24, inner fieldoffset 0/16; sizeof(JLWStatus)=260; sizeof(JLWResult{CNTuple{2, Tuple{CVector{:owned,Float64},Int64}}})=288, fieldoffset 0/264.",
